# Build context filter for app/auth-web/Dockerfile (its build context is this
# directory -- the repository-root .dockerignore does not apply to it, which is
# why this file has to exist per-stack). Mirrors app/web/.dockerignore.
#
# Two entries are load-bearing beyond context size:
#
#   node_modules / dist -- the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` runs *after* its own
#   `bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`. Without these excluded,
#   the host working copy's dependency tree (installed at some unknown time,
#   possibly with lifecycle scripts run) would be copied over the gated tree
#   the image build just produced, silently voiding both the lockfile pin and
#   the no-lifecycle-scripts guarantee (Shai-Hulud countermeasure -- see that
#   Dockerfile's build stage and .claude/rules/web.md).
#
#   .env / .env.* -- no local credential file is ever handed to the Docker
#   daemon as build context (CLAUDE.md「実行境界: runtime はコンテナのみ」: the
#   runtime image build takes no secrets, no ~/.npmrc, no cloud credentials).
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.git
.gitignore
*.md
coverage
.vscode
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
